-- A random Bool state (a two-state Markov chain, `trans fog`) passed as the
-- LEADING argument of a call whose callee recurses. Enumeration only
-- marginalises a curried call's last argument (curriedEnumerableCallee), so
-- the binding falls through to the set-valued witness engine, which cannot
-- propagate the observation through the recursive call and refuses: "set-valued
-- witness construction failed for the binding of 'l_11_fog' ... neither
-- point-invertible ... nor deterministic given scope". With the arguments
-- swapped (`cont n (trans fog)`) the state is enumerated and the program
-- reaches decreasing-recursion-refused-as-generate-fallback's refusal instead.
-- Found by the publication-exploration rare-event probe (runs2.ppl, a run of
-- consecutive misses under Markov-switching fog). Verified at 4f496c1 on dev.
-- Docs task random-leading-argument-into-recursion-refused.
-- Idealized: p(True) = 0.2 + 0.8 * 0.2 = 0.36.
expect-failure: refused "set-valued witness construction failed"
